# What the AX.25 STATION image is: the modules it executes in place, and
# the number of kernel processes it needs.
#
# One: the init loads Sys, which is built in, and Radiocal, which is
# this.  It runs no commands, because it runs no shell -- at NPROC 7 the
# three kprocs #a starts and a shell will not both fit, and a station
# whose job is a link does not need a prompt.  See
# os/inferno/init/armv7max25.b.
#
# The counterpart of that: the shell image's list is 347190 bytes of
# decoded arrays and this one is 9999, and the station init is 19440
# bytes bigger than the shell init.  With the shell image's list a
# station image came to 914264 bytes against a ceiling of 901120 and
# would not convert -- see the i$CONF.hex rule in the mkfile.
#
# A module left out of here is still in the root as its raw .dis and
# still not runnable on this part; image-armv7minit says why.
XIPDIS=\
	lib/radiocal.dis\

# Seven, and this number is why the file carries it.  Attaching a packet
# device to #a starts three kprocs; at five the station prints
# "addr N0CALL-1" and then "no procs for kproc" for ever, which is a
# board that looks like it booted.  Three kprocs is three slots whatever
# else is running.
NPROC=7

# The pool split, 50/49/1, which is what the comment in the conf records
# being measured at a shell prompt: main holds about 75K there and the
# Dis heap the rest.  image-armv7mstyx says why a satellite wants the
# opposite.
MAINPCNT=50
HEAPPCNT=49
IMAGEPCNT=1
